    "preamble": "Ashok Kumar Jha vs The State Of Maharashtra on 7 September, 2023 Author: N. J. Jamadar Bench: N. J. Jamadar 911-aba-2533-202 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.2533 Of 2023 Ashok Kumar Jha ...Applicant vs. The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent Ms. Anuj Tiwari a/w. Mr. Rahil Kazi, for the Applicant Mrs. Sharmila Kaushik, App, for the Respondent/State. Mr. V.S. Waghare, Pc, Ozar police station present. Coram : N. J. Jamadar, J. Date : September 07, 2023 P.C.: 1. Heard the learned counsel for the applicant and the learned App for the State. 2. This application is preferred seeking pre-arrest bail in connection with C.R. No. 150 of 2023 registered at Ozar police station for the offences punishable under sections 188, 272, 273, 328 read with 34 of Indian penal Code, 1860 and sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(d), 3(1)(zz)(iv) and 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006.",
